# Per-landing-page UI

**Must:** Every landing page can have a **different UI**. Do not assume one homepage layout, section set, or visual system fits all pages.

## Rules

1. Treat each route / landing as its **own design contract** (screenshot, Figma, or brief for **that** page)
2. Section order, hero style, cards, footer, motion, and density **may differ** per page
3. Reuse brand tokens (`@/config/brand`, CSS vars) and primitives (`ui/*`) when they fit; **do not** copy another page’s layout just because it exists
4. New landing → thin `src/app/<route>/page.tsx` + `src/components/<landing>/` + `src/data/<landing>.ts`; still mobile-first
5. Shared Header/Footer only when that page’s design includes them; variants allowed
6. Multi-page images: label **which landing**, implement that page only
7. Still follow structure + mobile (`structure-components-responsive.mdc`)

## Never

- Force Home section order onto another landing
- “Make it consistent with home” unless the user or design asks
- Merge unrelated landings into one component dump
